    "body": "Thanks for the tag @annevk. I have been chatting with Steve Workman at Mozilla (sorry, don't know his github) and his team was going to look into at least throwing a warning when window.opener is modified across origins (I think IE does this already).\n\n@mikewest Here is the original bug I filed: https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=28821 (I suspect this PR should resolve that). Also it looks like http://crbug.com/69267 is related to http://crbug.com/168988\n\nI just closed my PR on the wrong repo.\n\nRegarding the proposal, I had thought about using \"noopener\" keyword but I think \"newcontext\" might be a bit more explicit. Ultimately we don't _only_ want window.opener to be nullified, right? I think there is a desire to also do all of the other things (it might be hard to explicitly list everything though) associated with a new browsing context.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
